WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.273
Two draws without replacement
A bag contains three red balls and two blue balls, each equally likely to be
selected. Draw two successively without returning the first ball to the bag.

2
00:00:15.273 --> 00:00:29.182
First draw
We want both the first and second balls to be red. The first-draw probability
is three fifths because there are five balls in total.

3
00:00:29.182 --> 00:00:44.455
After a first red ball
Now suppose the first ball was red. Two red balls remain, and the total has
fallen to four. This information changes the probability on the second draw.

4
00:00:44.455 --> 00:00:57.909
Multiply along the same branch
For both events to occur, multiply the first probability by the second
conditional probability. We do not multiply three fifths by itself here.

5
00:00:57.909 --> 00:01:11.364
Simplify the result
The product is six twentieths. Cancel a factor of two to obtain three tenths,
equal to thirty percent of the equally likely cases.

6
00:01:11.364 --> 00:01:26.182
The model depends on replacement
This result depends on sampling without replacement, as the statement
specifies. If the ball were replaced, the counts would not fall and the
calculation would change.
